 ## Overview
-This method converts a signed distance field (SDF) value into a volumetric density for a box primitive, applying a sigmoid-based erosion at the boundaries to create smooth, anti-aliased edges and adding Perlin noise to roughen the surface [S1, unofficial]. It differs from standard SDF-to-density conversions by explicitly expanding the box geometry to define an erosion zone and combining axis-aligned sigmoid falloffs with spatial noise, rather than relying solely on a global distance threshold or simple alpha blending [S1, unofficial]. It builds on [SDF to Density Conversion](1282-sdf-to-density-conversion.md).
